<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! carriage.disk.removes ~ a pending removal answered toward the disk: the carrier leaves the wiki

`remove <uri>…` takes the vanished carrier out of its own bag's layer and retracts it to absent. Only where a lower layer holds the title too does the removal raise a kāpae: the confirmation line names that layer, the person's `y` approves it (the verb sends `kapae: true`), and `yes=true` alone leaves the island refusing `remove-raises-kapae` by name. Name one or more carriers, or `--all --count <n>`; an answer over more than one carrier names the count that stands pending. Where a commit took the file from the checkout, the answer names that commit and where its message says the substance went.

A terminal asks `Proceed? [y/N]`; a JSON call off a terminal needs `yes=true`. `face=N` answers a lit sibling's pending row without wearing it.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/shows`>>

!! shows ~ remove-one · remove-all

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`example` name=`remove-one` params=`uri/lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/example ~ retract the carrier from its bag`>>
<<has entity=`example` name=`remove-all` params=`all/true count/3 bag/lares ~ retract every pending row of the bag, the count named`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/takes`>>

!! takes ~ uri · all · count · bag · face · yes

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`arg` name=`uri` params=`takes/lar-address seat/1 as/<uri>… ~ one or more carriers a pending removal names`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`all` params=`kind/switch ~ every pending row of the named bag; rides count=`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`count` params=`takes/number ~ the count that stands pending, read from lares shore; an answer over more than one carrier names it`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`bag` params=`takes/bag-uri ~ narrow to one bag`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`face` params=`takes/handle-index ~ a lit sibling's shore, by handle index`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`yes` params=`kind/switch ~ name the intent for a call off a terminal; approves nothing by itself`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/gate`>>

!! gate ~ write · kapae

Testimony: the door checks; this slot grants nothing.

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`gate` name=`write` params=`who/hand ~ the carrier leaves the wiki's records; a kāpae over a lower layer needs the person's own y`>>
<<has entity=`gate` name=`kapae` params=`who/hand ~ a removal that raises a kāpae over a lower layer asks a person's y at the prompt; yes=true alone approves it not`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/refuses`>>

!! refuses ~ remove-raises-kapae · usage · count-missing · a-state-that-moved

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`remove-raises-kapae` params=`cure/[[carriage.disk.removes uri/<uri>]] ~ a lower layer holds the title too; answer y at a terminal to raise the kāpae`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`usage` params=`cure/[[carriage.disk.removes uri/<uri>]] ~ name a carrier, or --all with --count; --all beside carriers refuses`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`count-missing` params=`cure/[[carriage.disk.removes all/true count/3]] ~ an answer over more than one carrier names the count that stands pending`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`a-state-that-moved` params=`~ an answer names the state its giver read (a standoff's key, or the count that stands pending); where that state moved, the island refuses by name and nothing changes`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/answers`>>

!! answers ~ removed · aborted

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`band` name=`removed` params=`exit/0 fields/[[uri retiredBy]] ~ the carrier left its bag; retiredBy names the commit that took the file, where one did`>>
<<has entity=`band` name=`aborted` params=`exit/1 ~ the person answered no at the prompt`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

